<title>INDIA: Banque Indosuez cuts Indian prime lending rate.</title>
<headline>Banque Indosuez cuts Indian prime lending rate.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banque Indosuez is reducing its Indian prime lending rate to 17.25 percent per annum from 19.0 percent effective November 6, an official at its Bombay office said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>He said the maximum spread over the prime rate would be 5.0 percent. The cut follows similar reductions by several other banks after the central bank's monetary policy statement on October 19 which boosted liquidity.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
